# Serve the hosted games meta-schema with an explicit JSON content type.
#
# The schema is reachable at its declared $id
# (https://randsum.dev/schemas/v1/randsum.json) and editors fetch it via a
# `$schema` reference, so the content type has to be application/json rather
# than whatever the host guesses.
#
# This duplicates the [[headers]] block in netlify.toml on purpose, and only
# until Netlify is decommissioned. `_headers` is understood by BOTH Netlify and
# Cloudflare, so during the migration this one file keeps the rule correct on
# whichever host is serving. Deleting the netlify.toml block instead would have
# been tidier and riskier — it would change behaviour on the site that is
# currently live, to fix a site that is not yet serving anyone.
/schemas/*
  Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
